    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Collins O’Meara Auctioneers are delighted to introduce this exceptional property to the market in a beautiful scenic location within the Blackwater Valley.  Nestled in a truly magnificent setting adjoining the Glenaprechan stream as it enters the River Blackwater, the property benefits from a blend of quality pasture, natural woodland and mature landscaped gardens, all set on 1.71 acres.  Accessed via a stone gated entrance, the site offers both privacy and tranquility, all within 5 mins of Kilworth village.\r\n        \r\nThe residence was constructed in 2005 with a unique Scandinavian style finish incorporating the comforts and efficiencies of modern day living.  Accommodation is both bright and spacious throughout, with an abundance of windows allowing natural light to flow through the home. The ground floor comprises of a welcoming entrance hall, well-appointed kitchen/living area with a beautiful vaulted ceiling, spacious sunroom with feature patio door to paved outdoor space, downstairs bedroom and W.C.  Upstairs, first floor offers two further generously-sized rooms and bathroom, making it ideal for family living.  Teak windows and doors, vaulted ceilings, teak fascia and soffit plus quarry slate roof are just some of the finishes setting this property apart.  \r\n\r\nSurrounding gardens and curtilage have been tastefully maintained by the current owners, creating a mature and attractive outdoor space with potential for further development.  Natural stone patio areas and walkways with deer park fencing are woven between landscaped garden areas, and raised beds, all perched on an elevated position overlooking a post and rail fenced paddocked field which lies below the residence.  Endless potential is on offer, be it horticulture, hobby farming or equine interests.  Originally designed to be a hunting / shooting lodge, the property has the added benefit of a block-built stable area with two large stables, tack room and parking area. Wildlife in the area is second to none with an abundance of red squirrels, otters, herons, buzzards and pine martins all making Woodbrook Lodge their home.  Feeding time for the dozens of red squirrels from the kitchen window is a sight to behold, as well as observing the pine martins in their nest box in the trees.\r\n\r\nEfficiency is to the fore and the property benefits from a custom designed wood-block heating system operating underfloor heating . The system is based on a wood gasification boiler, helping to keep electricity costs to a minimum.  \r\n\r\nThis tranquil setting, combined with stunning countryside views and a truly unique residence, \r\nmakes this property a highly attractive opportunity for a wide range of purchasers.  \r\n\r\nViewing is a must to be fully appreciated.\r\n\r\nServices\r\nWood Gas Boiler with underfloor heating system. \r\nPrivate water well.  \r\nPrivate Septic Tank."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Conservatory\t\r\n3.68m x 2.83m\t\r\nTile floor, vaulted ceiling, access to patio area, power point.\r\n\r\nLiving Room / Kitchen\t\r\n7.03m x 4.33m\t\r\nTile floor, solid fuel cast iron stove  with roll steel surround, floor level kitchen units, integrated oven/hob, power points, T.V. point,  custom-made window shutters, vaulted trussed ceiling.\r\n\r\nCloak Room\t\r\n2.36m x 1.29m\t\r\nTile floor, water cylinder, plumbed for washing machine, power point.\r\n\r\nBedroom\t\r\n6.10m x 3.60m\t\r\nTile floor, built-in wardrobes, double French doors to patio, power points, T.V. point.\r\n\r\nBathroom\t\r\n2.11m x 3.23m\t\r\nTile floor,  W.H.B., W.C., power shower unit, bidet.\r\n\r\nBedroom\r\n4.41m x 3.71m\t\r\nCarpet floor, en-suite, built-in storage area, power-points. \r\n\r\nBedroom\t\r\n3.89m x 3.23m\t\r\nCarpet floor, built-in storage unit, power-points, T.V. point."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Unique one-off property offering potential purchasers a rare opportunity to acquire their dream home.\r\nLarge site and grounds extending to  c. 1.71 acres, consists of pasture, woodland and landscape gardens.\r\nHigh-end finishes throughout including Lismore sandstone patio areas, stone walls and walkways, deer park fencing, natural slate roof, vaulted timber ceilings, teak fascia and soffit, custom-built window shutters and much more.\r\nCirca 0.75 acre grassland paddock, securely fenced with post and rail fencing with natural stream boundary.\r\nBlock built stable block consisting of two stables and feed store.\r\nCut stone built entrance with electric gates and intercom.\r\nPrivate water well to depth of 160 feet.\r\nHighly efficient wood gasification boiler with underfloor heating.\r\nExcellent location only 2 miles from Kilworth village and 2.5 miles to M8 Interchange.\r\nHigh speed internet connection available, ideal for remote working.\r\nFully wheelchair accessible both internally and externally.\r\nFull CCTV security and alarm system throughout.\r\nSolid reinforced concrete built garage with car pit and electricity laid on.\r\nTailor-made for country pursuits like hunting, horse-riding, fishing, shooting and water activities."
      },
